# Later

## Tool approval prompts
pi runs bash, edit and write without asking. Add an optional approval step:
- A pi extension with a `tool_call` handler that returns `{ block: true, reason }`
  when the user declines (see .claude/skills/pi/sessions.md, "Permissions and trust").
- The handler asks the app over the sidecar protocol and waits for the answer.
- UI: approve / deny inline on the tool row; a setting for which tools ask
  (e.g. always ask for bash, never for read).

## Project trust prompt
Sessions open folders as untrusted, so project `.pi/` extensions and settings
never load. Ask once per folder and save the answer in pi's trust store.

## MCP server sign-in
Remote MCP servers that use OAuth show "Needs sign-in", but nothing signs in.
pi-mcp-adapter has `/mcp-auth <server>`; run it from the host (like
`/mcp reconnect`) and open its browser URL the way provider sign-ins do.
Check first how it reports the URL without a UI (.claude/skills/pi/mcp.md).
